 "text": "Hey there, how are you? You can use cord organizer that hangs on the wall just above the desk. They' easy to use and keep the cables out of the way. It' called a cord organizer. It hangs on the wall just above the desk and keeps the cables out of the way. Not at all. It plugs into a wall socket and comes down over a rod that you screw into the desk. It only takes a few minutes. Then use a power strip near the desk and plug it in. Then only one cable goes under, and it' easy to plug in. You can use cord shorteners on those. They' little clips that make the cables shorter without cutting them.",
